    "body": "Hmm, what about if you don't set the ruby version with `rbenv local <version>` but only use `.ruby-version`? This is the way I usually set it. Here's my test:\r\n\r\n```\r\n❯ mkdir test\r\n❯ cd test\r\n❯ touch test.rb\r\n~/test via 💎 v2.6.3\r\n❯ echo 2.6.5 > .ruby-version\r\n~/test via 💎 v2.6.3\r\n❯ rbenv local\r\n2.6.5\r\n~/test via 💎 v2.6.3\r\n```\r\nSo I'd expect that after creating `.ruby-version` the prompt would change to `2.6.5`.",
