    "body": "As it is currently implemented, the Ruby version is derived from running `ruby -v`. I'm not a Ruby user myself, but I'd imagine that setting the version in `.ruby-version` should change the version of `ruby` run, based on your current directory.\r\n\r\nHow do you use `ruby` after `rbenv` has changed the version you're using?",
