    "body": "I see. Looks like if there's a `.ruby-version`, it will only be respected by `ruby -v` if you execute that on the `rbenv`-managed ruby. Following along with my test from above:\r\n\r\n```\r\n~/test via 💎 v2.6.3\r\n❯ ruby -v\r\nruby 2.6.3p62 (2019-04-16 revision 67580) [universal.x86_64-darwin19]\r\n\r\n~/test via 💎 v2.6.3\r\n❯ rbenv exec ruby -v\r\nruby 2.6.5p114 (2019-10-01 revision 67812) [x86_64-darwin18]\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
